## Topic(s) Explored
- **consciousness-disconnect**: Audited the 8-way convergence claim for C ≈ 0.50 as the consciousness threshold. Investigated independence of the 8 approaches, checked external theories (IIT, GWT), and reviewed the neuroscience literature on anesthesia phase transitions.

## Key Findings
- **consciousness-8way-convergence-audit.md**: The 8-way convergence is largely constructed, not discovered. At most 1 of 8 approaches (anesthesia empirical) has external grounding, and even that doesn't directly measure C = 0.50. IIT has no threshold; GWT has no 0.50 value; 5 approaches are framework-internal. The function f(γ, D, S) is never algebraically specified — only threshold conditions are given. The physics C(ρ) and consciousness C = f(γ, D, S) are structurally different constructions sharing a name.

